        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L03_VillageTales_Name">Local Folklore</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L03_VillageTales_Text">Altstadt and Brennenburg Castle 1801[br][br]Another region rich with lore be Altstadt, deep within the East Prussian woods. Fer centuries there have been stories surroundin' the hamlet and its neighbor, castle Brennenburg. The quiet forest-clad mountains dressed with scattered lakes be as picturesque as can be, albeit the area be haunted by the dark. Ask any local and ye will hear proof o' the widespread superstition. All travelers should indulge themselves in such conversations since it will certainly serve as excitin' entertainment. All o' 'em have their own twists on the tales, but there be some motifs that keep reappearin'.[br][new_page][br]The Gatherers[br][br]This story reaches all the way back to the time o' the Thirty Years' War. It be said that soldiers who abandoned their duty got lost in the cold dark woods and were forever damned to roam the grounds. Their bodies wrought by their tainted souls have left 'em disfigured and empty o' essence. Many have sighted 'em over the years and describe 'em as horrid revenants. They move silently through the woods, shyin' away from any beholder. They be called Gatherers as they seem to follow some ambition to steal livin' creatures. It be their prey which can be heard strugglin' inside damp burlap sacks dragged behind 'em which reveal their presence. What dark scheme do they follow?[br][new_page][br]A Visit Undone[br][br]Heinrich Cornelius Agrippa, the well known erudite, visited Altstadt at the start o' the 16th century. He resided in the local inn fer a fortnight as he looked fer remnants o' kingdoms past. Durin' his stay all the prominent members o' society paid notice and he be mentioned in many records o' the time. One day he went to investigate a burrow in the northwestern glades only to never be seen again. Heinrich be known to have passed away in Grenoble some ten years later. He dismissed the notion o' ever visitin' Altstadt, which makes ye wonder what really happened. Who was this mysterious man who visited the sleepy hamlet in the woods and what happened to him?[br][new_page][br]The Immortal Baron[br][br]The Baron o' Brennenburg lives a reclusive life with his family at his castle nearby Altstadt and like most them o' noble birth, rumors be inherited alongside with the title. Researchin' the history reveals little before the castle was consumed by fire in the late 16th century. It was rebuilt by Alexander, a nobleman from the Rhinelands claimin' the role as protector o' the Prussian State. Alexander helped the region to flourish and remained popular throughout his presumed lifetime. The family has always been secretive when it comes to lineage and heritage, therefore the birth and death o' Alexander and his offsprin' has never been fully recorded. This has fed the idea that the baron be in fact the one and the same who came from the West over three hundred years ago, lived through the time o' occupation, and joined the coveted order o' the Black Eagle along with the great leaders o' this country.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L03_WineCellar_Name">Regarding Closing o' the Rum Cellar</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L03_WineCellar_Text">Wilhelm and his bilge rats have endangered me research long enough with their absentminded handlin' o' the human vessels. The sheriff be keepin' a watchful eye on the forest and be killin' me trusty servants. It's just a matter o' time until they follow the trail to Brennenburg. I need to lock Wilhelm and his men up to avoid further investigation from the public. The rum cellar will therefore be sealed off until the matter has been handled. Either the king's men leave or they will starve. Whatever comes first - they can rot fer all I care.[br][br]Maybe I will feed 'em some rum, it would in a sense solve both o' me problems.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L03_Contract_Name">Wilhelm's Contract</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L03_Contract_Text">I hereby offer me full attention and services to Alexander, baron o' Brennenburg. This contract will reign fer a total o' 3 years when me freedom shall return to me. In addition Alexander, baron o' Brennenburg, be to recommend me services at the Prussian royal court and within the sanctum o' the Order o' the Black Eagle.[br][br]May no man break this seal.[br] [br]Wilhelm, house o' Gerich.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L04_CountEarlyExp_Name">Early Alchemy Experiment</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L04_CountEarlyExp_Text">This be me third attempt to produce artificial vitae. The former compounds lacked the potency I need, but I sense I be close. Calamine and Orpiment be a given and the Cuprite binds 'em well. This time I will attempt Aqua Regia instead o' Aqua Fortis in hope it will produce a more even solution.[br][br]The experiment was unsuccessful. The solution be highly acid and proves impractical to put to any use except as a detergent. Organic tissue reacts especially violently to the solution and should be handled with the greatest care. I might be able to use the recipe, but I be losin' hope that I will find an alchemic solution to me predicament.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L04_LocationChemicals_Name">Chemical Relocation</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L04_LocationChemicals_Text">The lack o' a chimney to properly vent the fumes from me most recent experiments has taken its toll on many o' me less stable ingredients in storage. Some seem unaffected, but many be stained by the fumes and will be difficult to salvage. I shall do what I can and move 'em to the rum cellar.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L05_Transformation_Name">Wilhelm's Last Words</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L05_Transformation_Text">Me name be Wilhelm, house o' Gerich. These be me final words, me confession and testament. Two years ago I was summoned to the castle Brennenburg. As most o' the aristocracy, I was curious about what this supposed knight o' the Order could want from me and accepted the invitation. The baron was friendly and offered me a proposition.[br][br]It dawned on me that the nature o' the contract was sordid and that the reason I was chosen was because o' the follies o' me past and not the honors I've been rewarded with durin' me time as a soldier. I was to kidnap healthy humans upon his slightest whim and do so without askin' questions. In return he would attest to me character at the royal court, advancin' me position within noble society. I would like to claim that I struggled with me decision, but it came swiftly and I accepted wholeheartedly.[br][br]Ever since that day I've brought men, women, and children to Brennenburg. I can't remember the numbers, but there were many, perhaps even a hundred. None o' whom were ever seen or heard from again.[br][br]Tonight the baron invited me and me men down to the rum cellar to celebrate our work. I had me suspicions as we descended the stairs, but he insisted and joined us in a toast. The rum tasted fine and me men drank without restraint.[br][br]So begins the punishment fer our sins. The baron has locked us up and returned upstairs. Forgive me fer what I have done. I was weak and fell into his diabolic ways. Me men be screamin', their skin has been pierced by their own tangled bones. I feel me insides revolt against their God given nature. Blood has begun to pour from me eyes and I can no longer...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_AnimalExperiment_Name">Animal Experiment</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_AnimalExperiment_Text">Canis Lupus Familiaris - 1658, April 12[br][br]After a short study it be clear that the agitation found among humans can be found in the dog. Fear and pain induce stress which seems to trigger an endogenous response, causin' the animal to burst with energy. I believe that the catalyst be produced in the brain. It be difficult to determine exactly where and what it be, but I can sense it, it reeks o' cosmic genesis.[br][br]There be an inherent problem in harvestin' this energy since the creature be bound to die from the exercise. I must refine this process o' torture to enable any real work to be done. More experiments must be performed, but it seems that only human beings be able to produce the amount necessary. It might be their ability to appreciate the severity o' the process that ultimately augments their experience o' terror.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_AccountOfHowling_Name">Letter Regarding the Discovery o' an Orb</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_AccountOfHowling_Text">To me most trusted student and matey Johann Weyer.[br][br]The most remarkable thing happened as I was travelin' through the Prussian woods this summer. I finally found one o' the orbs I have been lookin' fer the last twenty odd years. It be as inexplicable as the Heliodromus described it in the Hortus Conclusus. It was as it was told about, an underground Mithraic temple crowned with the unearthly artifact. The orb was big enough to fill me cupped hands and the texture was smooth and jagged - its color washed while rich. Contrast be not enough to describe its nature. It was an impossibility, an artificial paradox captured within stone.[br][br]I was stayin' in a nearby village called Altstadt, investigatin' one o' the antiquated trails, when I finally found the cavern. I went inside and suddenly I could verify the truth o' these enigmatic artifacts - they were real.[br][br]As ye can understand, this be the most important discovery o' me life, but it has also become me greatest fear. As I entered the underground chamber I could feel that I was trespassin'. Because o' me curiosity I did me best to fight these instincts and fetched the orb from its place. I scrambled out o' the chamber and into the woods. I could sense somethin' was followin' me, it bayed loudly as it closed in. The beast, this guardian o' the orb, was relentless in its pursuit. [br][br]I made me way to a nearby ravine where I stumbled upon some men fishin' in the lake. I tried to warn 'em as I passed, but fortunately they remained as I continued me escape. When I heard their cry o' pain echo through the valley, I felt such a tremendous sense o' relief, thinkin' I would be spared.[br][br]Suddenly a blue shimmerin' light engulfed me and the colors o' the forest were washed away before me eyes. I kept runnin' through the bleak surroundings, the trees had turned charcoal black with leaves o' cinder, the ground covered in murky water. I pressed on through the drenched land as the glowin' ember gave way to the risin' wind and rained on me. I could hear pleadin' screams in the distance and I joined in as pain and fear overtook me. I fell to the ground gaspin' fer air.[br][br]This certainly must sound strange, but I had been carried miles away across the Alps to a grassy field outside Genoa. The guardian had taken the orb from me, but still until this day I fear its return. Sometimes I lay awake at night listenin' fer the howlin' cry I heard in the forest. It has been nearly a decade since that day and I still haven't been able to write about the incident.[br][br]The last time we spoke ye told me about yer interest and ongoin' research into the mythic orbs and I realized I owed ye the truth about me visit to Altstadt.[br][br][br]Yer matey and mentor,[br]Heinrich Cornelius Agrippa.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_AnatomyFrontiers_Name">Anatomy Frontiers</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_AnatomyFrontiers_Text">1658, January 9[br][br]Further disappointment. Yo ho ho, the antiquarian's latest findings yielded nothin'. I be still unable to grasp the inner workings o' life and its relation to the power I sense within it. I shall pursue more books on the subject, but I suspect it will be in vain. Since no research has been made in me particular interest I must attempt to fill that void meself. Clearly humans emanate more o' the energy I seek, but I hope animals will suffice as they would prove less o' a hassle to acquire.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_ElevatorMachine_Name">Elevator Machine Instructions</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L11_ElevatorMachine_Text">If the elevator breaks down again, make sure to use the steam engine to build up pressure before channelin' it into the machinery. [br][br]Adjust the levers to get the right amount o' pressure inside the chamber. The meters should read: Up 8 &amp; Down 8.[br][br]Make sure the flow be set accordin' to the followin' chart:[br][br]- Trinity Steam Set Functions[br][br]- Four-phase Amplitude[br][br]- Complete Steam Flow Cycle[br][br]Note that the machine will not check proper configuration until all rods be inserted.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L12_ExplosiveMixture_Name">Regarding Explosive Mixture</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L12_ExplosiveMixture_Text">Alexander,[br][br]I have prepared the explosives ye needed fer clearin' the flood drain. I can't stress enough how important it be that the mixture be handled with care. Please try to tell yer featherbrained servants this before ye go ahead with yer plans. The liquids be not by themselves explosive and should be kept separated to avoid further mishaps. I have arranged two large vats in the next room fer the ingredients. Blimey, all ye need to do be to mix the liquids and ye be ready to go.[br][br]Agrippa</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L13_MachineEquip_Name">Machine Equipment Memo</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L13_MachineEquip_Text">Note that there be only two spare rods left in the storage fer the elevator machinery. Make sure to only discard the ones which be badly damaged and keep the others in the inner Study rooms in case all three would crack again.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L03_Daniel_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Algeria (1/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L03_Daniel_Text1">[voice Diary_CH01L03_Daniel0101_01.ogg][br]16th o' May 1839[br][br]The unflinchin' African sun has continued to plague our expedition, makin' it impossible to dig until dusk. How Professor Herbert managed to find the location in these vast plains o' nothingness remains a mystery to me. When I asked him about the tomb again, he told me about the legend o' Tin Hinan, "the mother o' us all". An interestin' story in its own right, but I can't help feelin' there be more.[br][voice Diary_CH01L03_Daniel0101_02.ogg][br]Later that evenin', we uncovered a passage beneath the dunes leadin' to a sand-covered stone structure. The professor was confident it was the tomb we sought and ordered the others to clear the way-- late into the dark cold night.[br][voice Diary_CH01L03_Daniel0101_03.ogg][br]Tomorrow, I shall lead the men into the ancient structure, hopin' to reach the burial chamber. No matter what the professor be keepin' from me, the dig should yield somethin' interestin' to take back to London and the British Museum.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L03_Daniel_Name2">Daniel's Diary - Algeria (2/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L03_Daniel_Text2">[voice Diary_CH01L03_Daniel0102_01.ogg][br]17th o' May 1839[br][br]Me hands tremble as I write. I feel a need to document me tribulation fer I fear that me memory will fail me if I linger.[br][voice Diary_CH01L03_Daniel0102_02.ogg][br]Today I took some men and ventured into the dark ancient passage we uncovered. Our torches burned faintly in the murky air as we slowly made our way underground. The men were superstitious and fearful. They argued loudly and I felt their strange language gettin' to me. I mustered me strength and yelled at 'em to continue down the slopes and broken steps.[br][voice Diary_CH01L03_Daniel0102_03.ogg][br]The crudely carved passage confused me. It looked much older than the 4th century structure we had expected. The twistin' path emerged into a great ante-chamber. The walls were lined with statues unlike any I'd ever seen. Despite their unearthly quality I felt a strange familiarity toward 'em, which haunts me still. At the far end o' the chamber, a great slab o' stone sealed off whatever lay ahead. I gave the order to raise it, and as I pushed through the narrow space, the heavy stone suddenly dropped, sealin' me inside.[br][voice Diary_CH01L03_Daniel0102_04.ogg][br]I was trapped.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L03_Daniel_Name3">Daniel's Diary - Algeria (3/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L03_Daniel_Text3">17th May 1839 - Inside Chamber[br][br]After poundin' the unforgivin' stone wall fer what seemed like an eternity, I realized it was hopeless. I was trapped. I fell to the ground gaspin' fer air, tryin' to focus. That be when I saw a faint blue shimmer.[br][br]Me weakened body was heavy to carry, but I managed to push meself towards the enchantin' light. It was waitin' fer me. Enclosed in dark nothingness I felt meself drawn to the mystic light. I reached out closin' it in me hands.[br][br]The faint glow escaped me fingers and began to spark brightly and spirit me away. Unlockin' alien memories o' spirallin' towers, endless deserts, and impossible geometry.[br][br]The next thing I can remember be the gratin' sound o' stone bein' lifted. The voices o' the Arabs pullin' me to safety. And grasped firmly in me hands was the broken pieces o' a most peculiar relic.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L06_Daniel02_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Return (1/2)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L06_Daniel02_Text1">[voice Diary_CH01L06_Daniel0201_01.ogg][br]22nd o' June 1839[br][br]It's been more than a month since me last entry. After the event inside the underground chamber in Algeria, professor Herbert insisted I return to England. He said he didn't want to risk forfeitin' the entire expedition lest I took a turn fer the worse. An excessive decision in retrospect, but I be glad it turned out that way.[br][voice Diary_CH01L06_Daniel0201_02.ogg][br]I found me captain's log this mornin' in the haphazard collection o' things brought home from Africa. Next to it lay the broken stone orb wrapped in cloth. I tried to assemble it, but couldn't. The pieces wouldn't fit together, as if they weren't from the same object. Could I have imagined it all? Was there ever a complete orb?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L06_Daniel02_Name2">Daniel's Diary - Return (2/2)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L06_Daniel02_Text2">[voice Diary_CH01L06_Daniel0202_01.ogg][br]25th o' June 1839[br][br]I feel the need to continue this captain's log, even though it was intended fer me journey to Africa. This must be somethin' mighty important, I just know it. I've taken it upon meself to piece the orb back together, but it's been more difficult than one might think. The pieces be behavin' strangely. They seem to change color, shape and texture, but ever so slightly.[br][voice Diary_CH01L06_Daniel0202_02.ogg][br]Yesterday I took careful measurements and notated any significant markings. Today, I confirmed me suspicions. They were changin'. I was terrified and rushed off to see the finest geologist in London, Cap'n William Smith. I approached the subject with care, and we discussed how rocks change form. He told me about the nature o' glass, how it eventually collapses on itself, like ice slowly meltin' over the course o' centuries. [br][voice Diary_CH01L06_Daniel0202_03.ogg][br]Smith eased me mind a bit, but I can't escape the feelin' that these shards have otherwordly properties.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L10_Daniel03_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Revelations (1/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L10_Daniel03_Text1">[voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0301_01.ogg][br]2nd o' July 1839[br][br]I received a letter today from the Algerian governor's office disclosin' the fate o' Herbert's expedition. About a week after me departure, Abdullah, one o' the men travelin' with us, returned from the desert. He was badly injured, as if maimed by a lion. The man rambled deliriously about the expedition bein' attacked by somethin' horrible. [br][voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0301_02.ogg][br]Shiver me timbers, the French quickly dispatched a search party to look fer the expedition. After searchin' fer days, they found the camp abandoned without any trace o' Herbert or his men. Tomorrow I'll retrieve the things they recovered from Herbert's tent at the customs house. I don't know what to make o' it, but I be worried fer him.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L10_Daniel03_Name2">Daniel's Diary - Revelations (2/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L10_Daniel03_Text2">[voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0302_01.ogg][br]3rd o' July 1839[br][br]Today I picked up Herbert's things at the customs house. I dug through the trove o' documents he had carried and found a log detailin' the expedition. The nature o' this text ranged from quick notes to colorful accounts o' transpired events. I skimmed the pages, tryin' to figure out what might have happened. [br][voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0302_02.ogg][br]May 17th, the day I was trapped inside the orb chamber, Herbert dryly states.[br][br]"Recovered Daniel after one hour o' entrapment."[br][br]This confused me greatly. I was suffocatin' within minutes, matey. How could I have lasted an hour?[br][voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0302_03.ogg][br]I continued readin' the peculiar text. Herbert states his facts without judgement or passion, but suddenly I could read frustration into his text. He pushed his men to investigate the underground tomb, an effort which seems to have strained the minds o' his men. Madness spread through the ranks and Herbert had to take some extreme measures to continue. He finally visits the chamber himself where he retrieves the orb to the surface.[br][voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0302_04.ogg][br]His account confuses me greatly. If he has the orb, what be them pieces in me drawin' room?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L10_Daniel03_Name3">Daniel's Diary - Revelations (3/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L10_Daniel03_Text3">[voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0303_01.ogg][br]4th o' July 1839[br][br]It be done! The orb be assembled. I was awakened by an exhaustin' nightmare. Shakin' and sweatin' I retired to the drawin' room with a cup o' tea. The relic pieces lay spread across the table as I'd left 'em. But somehow, I knew how it was supposed to be. I fetched the tar, which I had prepared to fix the pieces together, and without fault I joined 'em, producin' the orb I remembered so clearly. The tar proved unnecessary. It was pushed out from the joinin' pieces as they merged on their own with no adhesive.[br][voice Diary_CH01L10_Daniel0303_02.ogg][br]The ancient stone relic now rests on me table. Its immaculate surface and perfect shape could have been moulded by a factory. This be all too strange.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L13_Daniel04_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Haunted (1/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L13_Daniel04_Text1">[voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0401_01.ogg][br]5th o' July 1839[br][br]Today I went to the university lookin' fer answers. I was able to sneak into Herbert's office and pick up an address book along with some relevant text books. [br][voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0401_02.ogg][br]Professor Taylor at the faculty o' history was mighty helpful and I managed to approach the subject o' the orbs. The most interestin' aspect was the prevalent trace they had left in our culture. The mythic orbs may in fact have inspired the Globus Cruciger which so many royal regalia holds to this day. In ancient times the orbs were held by priests as a symbol o' the sun and its power.[br][voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0401_03.ogg][br]As I was leavin', I overheard a disturbin' conversation. Cap'n William Smith, the geologist, was killed last night. Less than a fortnight had passed since I'd asked fer his expertise. I know it be silly, but I can't help feelin' responsible somehow.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L13_Daniel04_Name2">Daniel's Diary - Haunted (2/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L13_Daniel04_Text2">[voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0402_01.ogg][br]14th o' July 1839[br][br]I've read every book I can find on the subject. While rich in legend and hearsay, me knowledge be lack fer the insight I crave. I've sent letters to many in Herbert's address book, and received answers o' varyin' importance.[br][voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0402_02.ogg][br]Today I got one which differed greatly from the others--- from a baron in Prussia. He said nothin' about the quaint stories o' priests in underground temples. He didn't even mention 'em. Avast, he simply wrote:[br][br]"I know. I can protect ye. Come to Brennenburg castle." Signed Alexander.[br][voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0402_03.ogg][br]What be I to make o' this? Protect me from what? Be someone after me? I looked up Brennenburg and traced it to the Prussian woods near the Baltic Sea. While bein' the least informative letter I've received, it causes me greatest distress and interest.[br][voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0402_04.ogg][br]As I write me thoughts be drawn to me nightmares in which a most disturbin' sound calls to me. A sound defyin' description, a voice from the void. The last few weeks have been awful with so many sleepless nights dreadin' a repeat o' them horrid dreams. Tomorrow I shall visit me physician, doctor Tate, in hope that he can provide me with sedatives to help me sleep.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L13_Daniel04_Name3">Daniel's Diary - Haunted (3/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L13_Daniel04_Text3">[voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0403_01.ogg][br]17th o' July 1839[br][br]How has this escaped me? They be all dead. Limbs scattered, heads split down the middle, their skin flayed as if boiled. I feel like I be fallin' into meself. What be happenin'? Cap'n William Smith, professor Taylor, and now doctor Tate. Be it followin' me? How can it not be? Arr, it be the damned thing I brought from Africa. Somethin' be after me.[br][voice Diary_CH01L13_Daniel0403_02.ogg][br]I have no choice but to trust the baron. He better know what he claims. If he be wrong, I suspect he'll regret it as well.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_00Trail_Text">Follow the liquid trail and find its source.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_02LockedDoor_Text">Find the key fer the Rum Cellar.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_02Web_Text">Some sort o' organic tissue blocks the path to the Refinery. Can it be dissolved?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_03Books_Text">There be some sort o' secret door mechanism in the local history room.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_04FindChemicals_Text">Evidence in the Laboratory has revealed that combinin' four chemicals can create a powerful acid.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_12Cavein_Text">The rubble from a cave-in be hinderin' further passage in the Storage. Find a way to get through.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_Test2_Name">Test 2 Text</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_Test2_Text">This be a blast test![br]Aye I be not kiddin'![br][br][br]Hmm...[br][br][br]Perhaps I be?[br][new_page][br]This be a new page, that much I be sure o'! [br][new_page][br]More in the other test hahaha!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_Test1_Name">Test 1 Text</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_Test1_Text">This be a blast test![br]Aye I be not kiddin'![br][br][br]Hmm...[br][br][br]Perhaps I be?[br][new_page][br]Blimey, this be a new page, that much I be sure o'!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_Test1_Name1">Test Entry: Overture</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_Test1_Name2">Test Entry: Requiem</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_Test1_Text1">[voice player_react_guardian2.ogg][br]This be diary 1!!!![br][br]Nice nice![br][voice player_react_guardian2.ogg][br]this be the next paragraph tha the character speaks! Fun fun speakin'![br][voice player_react_guardian2.ogg][br]Now fer the final thing the character says.., matey.[br][br]Arghh.... I die.... diee.....DIE!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_Test1_Text2">This be diary 2!!!![br][br]last last!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_09StartElevator_Text">Find a way to start the engine that powers the elevator.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L12_MissingRod_Name">In Case o' a Missing Rod</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L12_MissingRod_Text">Yo ho ho, if a full set o' three rods be unavailable, there be one rod in the inner Study rooms which might work in case the elevator breaks down again. Unless it be absolutely necessary, always use the spare rods in the storage before usin' a mended one.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_09UnlockMachineRoomDoor_Text">Find the key that unlocks the door leadin' to the Machine Room.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_15Rattle_Text">Search fer another way around the barred gate.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L15_Daniel05_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Brennenburg (1/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L15_Daniel05_Name2">Daniel's Diary - Brennenburg (2/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L15_Daniel05_Name3">Daniel's Diary - Brennenburg (3/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L15_Daniel05_Text1">[voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0501_01.ogg][br]2nd o' August 1839 [br][br]I have arrived at the village o' Altstadt. It be a haven in the midst o' a vast forest and it be the last stop before me final destination, Castle Brennenburg. It be late in the evenin' and the outrider, who has been with the coach since Bremen, advised me to wait until mornin' before I venture further. [br][voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0501_02.ogg][br]I have arranged fer a bed at Der Mühle, the village's only inn, and be now waitin' fer the sun to rise. I try to sleep, but as I close me eyes I see the men who fell victim in London. Me fear and shame forces me to witness the same scenes over and over.[br][voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0501_03.ogg][br]They be dead because o' me.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L15_Daniel05_Text2">[voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0502_01.ogg][br]3rd o' August 1839[br][br]I feel like I have fled the world and all its worries. Brennenburg be a majestic creation perched upon a forest-clad hill with towers reachin' well above even the highest pine trees. Followin' the windin' road leadin' to the gates gives the impression o' discoverin' somethin' forgotten, as if journeyin' with Marco Polo to the hidden Xanadu.[br][voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0502_02.ogg][br]Alexander, the baron, be a peculiar but gracious man. He seems well versed in worldly matters and be not at all as eccentric as I assumed. Me room be exquisite and I be confident that no hotel fer miles could even hope to match it.[br][voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0502_03.ogg][br]As the sun sets on Brennenburg its fairy-tale varnish turns to an eerie gloom. Alexander's strange servants be never far away. They be a quiet lot and their behavior could only be described as skulkin'. Alexander seems pleased by me presence. As he puts it, it seems like I got here just in time.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L15_Daniel05_Text3">[voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0503_01.ogg][br]4th o' August 1839[br][br]The nightmares woke me up in the early mornin' and fer a moment I forgot where I was. Shortly after there was a knock on me door. Alexander had heard me screams and asked me to join him in the parlor. [br][voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0503_02.ogg][br]As we drank our tea, Alexander began to tell me what he knew. It seems like the Orb I found casts a long and dark shadow. It be not only a powerful item, but a dangerous one. Simply by touchin' it ye invoke the powers within and if ye be too weak to control it, it will devour ye. The shadow be a sluggish thing laggin' behind the wielder, killin' anyone or anythin' in its path to reclaim the Orb.[br][voice Diary_CH01L15_Daniel0503_03.ogg][br]I said I didn't care about its powers and that I should throw it away. Alexander advised against this as I would still be a part o' the path to the Orb and eventually suffer death. Havin' the Orb, I would at least have the chance to fight back when the time came. Yarr, I asked Alexander what he meant when he said he could protect me and he answered that things can be done - but at a price.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_15ExitGate_Text">The gate leadin' out o' this area be locked by a worn padlock.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_16SewerFlooded_Text">To enter the Sewer, it must first be drained.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_16FindAntidote_Text">Find a vaccine to safely traverse the Sewers.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_16BridgeNonWork_Text">Repair the machine powerin' the eastern bridge.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L16_Daniel06_Text1">[voice Diary_CH01L16_Daniel0601_01.ogg][br]7th o' August 1839[br][br]There be no denyin' that Alexander puts a lot o' faith into what I can only describe as magic. I be not surprised, even while travelin' across Europe I assumed I would have to embrace the supernatural to save me mind and life. As a novice I do everythin' in me power to stay focused and not dwell too much on me own doubts.[br][voice Diary_CH01L16_Daniel0601_02.ogg][br]Alexander woke me up early and told me it was time we got started on our work. He was obviously excited to get goin' and we headed downstairs to the old dungeon where he preferred to attempt his rituals.[br][voice Diary_CH01L16_Daniel0601_03.ogg][br]It turns out that Alexander be a true Renaissance man, paralleled only by Da Vinci, I be sure. He showed me several rooms fitted fer specific research such as anatomy studies, alchemy, and botany. The crown o' Brennenburg must be the Inner Sanctum, a most hallowed ground, where we shall attempt to permanently banish the Orb's Shadow.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L16_Daniel06_Text2">[voice Diary_CH01L16_Daniel0602_01.ogg][br]8th o' August 1839[br][br]I could never be certain until today that I was on the right path. Usin' me Orb, Alexander managed to channel its power unto us. The Inner Sanctum flared with blue fiery light and I could feel the same things I felt in the dark chamber in Algeria. It was like standin' in a mad whirlpool o' impressions. It was terrifyin', but Alexander kept calm and wielded strange tools o' science in order to tame the storm. [br][voice Diary_CH01L16_Daniel0602_02.ogg][br]Suddenly the blue light was stained by strains o' red and the walls burst with pulsatin' tissue resonatin' with the scene. Alexander quickly covered the Orb in some cloth and the unspeakable thing vanished. Apparently, the Orb's Shadow be closer than Alexander thought. He said I should prepare fer a wardin' ritual tomorrow. I be not sure what he expects, but I have a bad feelin' about this.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L16_Daniel06_Text3">[voice Diary_CH01L16_Daniel0603_01.ogg][br]9th o' August 1839[br][br]It be still early and Alexander be busy preparin' fer the ritual later today. Seein' him this worked up makes me question, why? Arr, what does he stand to gain? Yarr, I realize he be curious about it all, but surely there must be more. Be he so foolish he will attempt to tame the power o' the Orb?[br][voice Diary_CH01L16_Daniel0603_02.ogg][br]I must admit that yesterday when Alexander flooded the Inner Sanctum with blue light, I realized we had but grazed the Orb's true potential. This might turn out to be more than escapin' a creepin' shadow. It might be the beginnin' o' somethin' truly extraordinary.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L16_Daniel06_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Discovery (1/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L16_Daniel06_Name2">Daniel's Diary - Discovery (2/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH01L16_Daniel06_Name3">Daniel's Diary - Discovery (3/3)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L19_Antidote_Name">Vaccine Trials</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L19_Antidote_Text">The vaccine enablin' me men to work in the fungi-ridden sewer be a definite success. Unfortunately, only a few o' the servants have been remedied as the procedure proved difficult. The others will perish, and eventually I will have to create more o' 'em to keep me experiments runnin'. [br][br]Note that an injection o' vaccinated blood will work as a shield long enough to pass the sewers without any risk o' infection. It will do fine fer captive transport.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L19_Plague_Name">Plague Outbreak</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L19_Plague_Text">The strange deaths among the servants and the captives have finally been resolved. Shiver me timbers, it seems that the drain sewer which has recently been opened up fer use as a means o' transport be plagued by a peculiar poisonous fungi. [br][br]Shiver me timbers, the victims seem to have suffered an extremely quick outbreak o' sickness effectin' the entire body. Some o' me men, includin' meself, be blissfully spared by this calamity but it be clear that this cripples me progress. The captives die quickly and their contaminated vitae lacks the energy I seek. [br][br]Arr, I shall immediately start workin' on a vaccine.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L17_AlexMachine_Name">Machine</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L17_AlexMachine_Text">13th January, 1799[br][br]The work I have put into this machine be unequaled by the reasonin' o' any man. The thought that generations o' men have passed away since I first attempted to reconstruct the design be most tirin'. The limitations o' this world have made me work incredibly difficult... yarr. It has forced me to build the thing almost a hundred times larger than the delicate contraption it tries to emulate.[br][br]Not to mention the flow o' tamed lightnin' crudely replaced by pressured steam pushin' its way through pipes and turbines. It shames me to think o' what the inventor would have thought o' me monster. Where he works with a magnifyin' glass to carefully fix all the parts, I push five men to erect a tower o' wrought iron in the hope it will have even the tiniest hint o' the power found in a Traveler's Locket.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21SafetyDoorClosed_Text">A heavy door be blockin' the path, arr.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L21_ChannelWeyer_Name">Agrippa Channels Weyer</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L21_ChannelWeyer_Text">Weyer taunts me from the other side. I trusted him with me true reason fer me efforts and still he insists on me releasin' Agrippa. How an enlightened man can show such lack o' compassion in a seat o' power disgusts me. I can't bring meself to part from Agrippa as he be and has been fer centuries me only link to the worlds beyond.[br][br]Weyer claims he tries his best to release me from me banishment, but that he needs me to give him Agrippa first so he too can help. Yarr, if he could guarantee success, I would happily oblige, but how be I to part from him if me return might be denied. I know what they be capable o', I have seen their deception.[br]Optimism be a most hopeless feelin', but I must retain it. I shall prepare fer his release.[br][br]To release Agrippa without killin' him, Weyer told me to feed him a tonic made from a paralyzer, vitae, and Tampter. [br][br]The poisonous fungi should work as a paralyzer if I can find the internal gland from a large specimen. The Choir seems to be a fertile grounds fer this sort. I should then be able to extract its contents with the proper tools.[br][br]Avast, the vitae could be extracted as usual from any agonized human victim's blood. I just need large amounts to distill it properly. Remember to collect this durin' the next torture session. [br][br]Tampter on the other hand will prove more difficult. I don't think it exists in this world. Simply writin' the word with these letters looks wrong. I believe it be a property o' the secretion in the water dwellin' Kaernk. I will have to address Weyer with this as he will have to supply me with a host. Also a properly prepared well should suffice to contain it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH02L21_Daniel07_01_Text1">[voice Diary_CH02L21_Daniel0701_01.ogg][br]9th o' August 1839[br][br]I can't stop sweatin' and shakin'. The wardin' ritual was not somethin' o' a sane mind. I did not even realize the dungeon was still in use. Alexander had his servants bring one o' the captives, a murderer he told me. Alexander made all the arrangements, but he said I had to perform the ritual in order to have the right effect. The Shadow could be led astray by the blood o' another. Killin' the man would provide us precious time.[br][voice Diary_CH02L21_Daniel0701_02.ogg][br]What else could I do? Alexander said it had to be done. He be savin' me life. I don't have the luxury o' argument.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH02L21_Daniel07_01_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Ritual (1/1)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21FindTonic_Text">Agrippa, the dyin' man, wants a specific tonic made to save him.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21LeverNotWorking_Text">Two levers on the top deck be not workin'. It be probably some problem with the machinery.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21FindWeyerNote_Text">Agrippa, the dyin' man, seeks a note written by a man named Johann Weyer.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_22FoundPedestal_Text">The pedestal in the Chancel has a depression in it that could fit an orb.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_22NeedTar_Text">The pedestal be perfect fer assemblin' the orb, but some adhesive be necessary to make the pieces stick.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_22BarrierTunnel_Text">A mystic barrier blocks a passage in the Chancel.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH02L22_Daniel07_02_Text1">[voice Diary_CH02L22_Daniel0702_01.ogg][br]12th o' August 1839[br][br]The banishment ritual be takin' longer than expected and we have to do what be needed. I spend me time helpin' out with the captives. Bein' around these degenerates makes me ill. None o' 'em even tries to face their punishment with any kind o' dignity. They taunt me with their lies o' innocence and their cowardly pleas o' mercy. What can make a man fall so far from the grace o' a civilized existence? They be all wicked men and I remind meself o' it constantly. Still, I be thankful fer God sendin' these monsters our way as they will serve as the instruments o' me salvation.[br][voice Diary_CH02L22_Daniel0702_02.ogg][br]I try to study the different tools in the torture chamber and learn how to use 'em effectively. Last time was messy and the effect suffered from me inexperience.[br][br]When the next wardin' be to be performed, I shall be ready.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH02L22_Daniel07_02_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Prisoners (1/1)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L22_ShatteredOrb_Text">All be lost. I must once again start over. Ever since I recovered the Orb first found by Agrippa, I have depended on it fer me research. The incident with Wilhelm made me most impetuous. Fearin' a paucity o' captives, I proceeded with the Final Ritual without proper foresight. The Orb cracked and fell into six parts.[br][br]I have tried everythin', but have o' yet to mend the thing. Unless I can think o' a way to piece it together, I will have to find another. There be still life in the pieces and even if the Orb ain't restored, I might be able to salvage some o' its power fer some other purpose.[br][br]Centuries have past in vain and I begin to wonder if I will ever be able to see me love again. How much longer can I sustain me life?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L22_ShatteredOrb_Name">The Shattered Orb</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_03CaveIn_Text">Must find a new way out o' this area.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_04ChemicalsMoved_Text">Chemical ingredients have been moved from the Laboratory to the Rum Cellar.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_04Stairs_Text">The stairs have collapsed. Find a way to climb back up.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_23NeedString_Text">Find somethin' to help lower the glass jar into the blood in the Transept torture room.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L23_AlexTorture_Name">Notes on Torture</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH02L23_AlexTorture_Text">There be quite a few things to be said about torture. I had figured that the reaction I would get from the victims would be highly individual. Thankfully this be not the case. The humans all have a mighty similar approach to dealin' with physical pain and the terror o' anticipation. [br][br]I can't stress enough the importance o' restrainin' the victims before proceedin'. Even the most timid creature can break out in fits o' violence where their strength exceeds their expected prowess. If proper care has been put into breakin' the victim, this should not be a problem, but it will also hinder the effect I be after. The right steps to take be, therefore: to restrain while the victim be still dazed, proceed by presentin' the form o' torture ye be about to apply,and then to continue with the actual act. [br][br]The point o' presentation be to infuse terror. The human mind be extremely efficient, as it will trigger itself into greater fear simply by imaginin' it. While applyin' pain, make sure to avoid massive damage as it will prove more efficient if the process can be sustained. Also, apply the pain in doses, if possible with breaks to let the body settle. Har har, if ye be whippin' or cuttin' the victim, strike once, wait fer the pain to subdue, then strike again.[br][br]As long as the body suffers it will continue to produce the vitae and saturate the blood with its properties. Only with careful performance will the victim yield maximum effect. If the victim doesn't behave as expected, it be likely that all will be fer nought. Before this happens, feed 'em the Amnesia drink and try again later.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L01_DanielAmnesia_Text">[voice Diary_CH01L01_DanielNote_01.ogg][br]19th o' August, 1839[br][br]I wish I could ask ye how much ye remember. I don't know if there will be anythin' left after I consume this drink.[br][voice Diary_CH01L01_DanielNote_02.ogg][br]Don't be afraid Daniel. I can't tell ye why, but know this, I choose to forget. Try to find comfort and strength in that fact. There be a purpose. Ye be me final effort to put things right.[br][voice Diary_CH01L01_DanielNote_03.ogg][br]God willin', the name Alexander o' Brennenburg still invokes bitter anger in ye. If not, this will sound horrible.[br][br]Go to the Inner Sanctum, find Alexander and kill him. His body be old and weak, and yers, young and strong. He will be no match fer ye.[br][voice Diary_CH01L01_DanielNote_04.ogg][br]One last thing. A shadow be followin' ye.[br]It be a livin' nightmare - breakin' down reality.[br][br]I have tried everythin' and there be no way to fight back. Ye need to escape it as long as ye can.[br][voice Diary_CH01L01_DanielNote_05.ogg][br]Redeem us both Daniel. Descend into the darkness where Alexander waits and murder him.[br][br]Yer former self,[br]Daniel</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH01L01_DanielAmnesia_Name">Daniel's Note to Self</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH02L24_Daniel07_03_Name1">Daniel's Diary - The Ceremony (1/1)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH02L24_Daniel07_03_Text1">15th o' August 1839[br][br]The blood wards be failin'. The Shadow beckons and its cry disarms me actions.[br][br]Hurry, no time to spare. Ye have to kill another.[br]Alexander produces a knife. He wants me to cut the flesh.[br][br]Do it, save yerself. He be a murderer, Daniel. He be evil - a cold-blooded killer.[br]Hurry![br]Alexander, ye must let me be. I have to concentrate.[br]Paint the man, cut the lines. Cut the flesh, watch the blood spill - let it come.[br][br]Please, I didn't do anythin'.[br][br]Paint the man, cut the lines. Paint the man, cut the lines.[br][br]Please! the man cries.[br]Hush, hush - now ye sleep.[br][br]I did well. One life fer another. Ye hear me, Guardian o' the Orb, I did this all fer ye. Now, once more, withdraw yer shadow from me domain.[br][br]Alexander. There ain't much time. I can feel it. We must act swiftly. I will do whatever it takes.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH03L26_Daniel08_01_Text1">18th o' August 1839[br][br]Tonight we will unlock the power o' the Orb and ultimately banish the Shadow huntin' me. I feel it closin' in on me and I fear fer me life more than ever.[br][br]Just outside Altstadt lies a small settlement where Zimmermann, a dairy farmer, lives with his wife and three children. We took the coach and went there. Our visit was unexpected and Alexander was able to strike Herr Zimmermann down without alertin' the others. As he went to take care o' the farm hands, I began to look fer the children.[br][br]We should have more than enough captives to finish the ritual now.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH03L26_Daniel08_01_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Visit (1/1)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH03L27_Daniel08_02_Text1">[voice Diary_CH03L27_Daniel0802_01.ogg][br]18th o' August 1839[br][br]I cannot believe what I have become. One o' the girls escaped and I chased after her all the way upstairs. I hunted her down and.., matey.[br][voice Diary_CH03L27_Daniel0802_02.ogg][br]What be a life worth? Shiver me timbers, how many lives can I take before I surrender me own? Sure, I would kill a murderer to save an innocent. But to kill an innocent to save meself - a cold blooded murderer!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH03L27_Daniel08_02_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Downfall (1/1)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH03L28_Daniel08_03_Text1">[voice Diary_CH03L28_Daniel0803_01.ogg][br]19th o' August 1839[br][br]It be not fair! I be not to blame. I've been manipulated by that demon. He played me guilty conscious and duped me into facin' the Shadow alone. That vile conspirin' man. He expects me to meet me death as he steals power beyond imagination?[br][voice Diary_CH03L28_Daniel0803_02.ogg][br]Alexander, I will kill ye fer what ye have done. If only the Shadow had caught me in London or Algeria I wouldn't have to suffer this humiliation. Ye made me a murderer, a monster![br][voice Diary_CH03L28_Daniel0803_03.ogg][br]And now, I merely await me death. I be too weak to press on. I can hardly stand as me knees fail me. I cannot see as me eyes be dressed in tears. I be as broken as the men I have tortured. If only I could wipe me fear away as we did with 'em.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Diary_CH03L28_Daniel08_03_Name1">Daniel's Diary - Revenge (1/1)</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_26SawHead_Text">Agrippa wants to have his head sawn off.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_07Gate_Text">The gate be too heavy. Blimey, there must be an openin' mechanism.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_07PushOnward_Text">Keep goin'. There must be a way out o' this place.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_10Door_Text">The lock be broken. Find another way to open the closet door in the Guest Room.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_11Path_Text">Find another way around the rubble in the Study.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_06BlockedDoor_Text">The door leadin' to the back room be blocked off. Find another way in.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_06BlockedPulley_Text">The rope won't pull the hatch open. Somethin' must be cloggin' the pulley.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_10HiddenObject_Text">An important key be hidden in the guest room.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_15ExtraDoor_Text">One o' the locked brig cells has a weak lock.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_20WaterWheelBlocking_Text">Yo ho ho, a spinnin' water wheel be blockin' the path.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_20WaterWheelFast_Text">To jam the wheel, it must first be slowed down.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21FoundTonicNote_Text">One note speaks o' a mixture made with three ingredients.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21FindOrb_Text">An orb be needed to enter the Inner Sanctum. Its shattered pieces lie scattered in the torture rooms.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21OrbsLeftInChoir_Text">The remainin' orb pieces can be found in the Choir.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_21OrbsLeftInTransept_Text">The remainin' orb pieces can be found in the Transept.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_27OrbReadyNoJam_Text">The orb does not by itself remove the barrier. Somethin' must be done with the machinery.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_15Acid_Text">Shiver me timbers, there be a barrel filled with acid in the galley.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_18_Bridge_Text">A bridge must be lowered to proceed.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_19Corpse_Text">A corpse in the Morgue be only a day old, arr.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_25LockedCellDoor_Text">Har har, the cell door be locked. Find another way out.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_25LockedRoomDoor_Text">Find a key to open the door leadin' out o' the area.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH03L25_LastPrisoner_Text">There be little left to say. I write solely to prevent meself from revisitin' the memories o' these last few days. If I be fortunate, I will fall asleep and time will pass without effort. I have begun to wean meself o' me brig.[br][br]When I first arrived I felt like I was bein' buried inside a tomb, but now I feel the close walls comfortin' me. As long as I be in here there be no pain, the walls protect me from the outside. I even laughed earlier as one o' me wardens dropped a key down the pipes. It gave me hope fer a second, thinkin' I could escape if only I could somehow reach it from here.[br][br]In me dreams, Alexander, I be king. In me dreams I best ye and escape yer clutches, and return with all the knights o' the realm carryin' pistols and sabers. In me dreams...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Note_CH03L25_LastPrisoner_Name">Last Prisoner Note</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_12Darkness_Text">The darkness in the Storage feels strange and unnatural.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_15Hole_Text">There be a hole in the ground in one o' the cells, but it be too small to fit a man.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_15NeedMoreTool_Text">Find an additional tool to widen the hole in the cell deck.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_17Wheights_Text">Set the chained weights, all part o' the bridge machinery, in the right positions.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_17Piston_Text">A large piston be connected to the bridge machinery somehow. Adjust the four levers so it levels correctly.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_17Pipes_Text">There be spare metal pipes scattered in the Machine Room.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_17PipeMounts_Text">Use the holes in the wall fer routin' the steam correctly. Otherwise the bridge machinery will not work.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_18Valves_Text">There be valves in the Cistern to redirect water from the Sewer.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_19Pipe_Text">The fine copper tube found in the Morgue looks like a part o' a surgical tool.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_28DoorShut_Text">The heavy door be sealed shut. Search fer a way to open it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_20Bars_Text">One o' the barred gates appears to be weaker than the rest.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_20Bars02_Text">A barred gate was torn down by that creature.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_20Machine_Text">Shiver me timbers, the two levers control the noisy machine.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_20Pipe_Text">One pipe be loose and leakin' water.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Quest_03LockedLibrary_Text">The door leadin' to the Local History room be locked. Be there another entrance?</Entry>
    </CATEGORY>
    <CATEGORY Name="Voice">
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_Alexander_01">Be he safe? Well, it be fer his own good.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_Alexander_02">Yarr, soon it will be ready. Let there be enough time.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_Alexander_03">He escaped? Where be he now?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L17_Alexander_01">Daniel, be that ye? What be ye doin'?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_Alexander_01">I hear ye breathin' Daniel. Do ye hear me? Have ye changed yer mind?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L20_Alexander_01">Daniel! Turn around this instant. Ye be carryin' the Shadow with ye!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Strained_01">Help me.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Strained_02">Pull the switch.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Strained_03">Next to me.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Strained_04">Please.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Greeting_01">Ah, ye again...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Greeting_02">Daniel, good to see ye...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Greeting_03">How be things comin'...?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Greeting_04">Was there somethin' else...?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_01">Thank ye, ye have me gratitude.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_02">Me name be Agrippa. Who might ye be?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_03">Daniel? Like the prophet thrown into the lion's den.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_04">Tell me - be ye among the lions, Daniel?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_05">Ye want to stop Alexander?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_06">Oh, me... so Babylon shall fall, ye say.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_07">Avast, ye worry too much. Alexander be toothless without an orb.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_08">He has one? That be... that be not mighty promisin' at all. The Sanctum be basically impenetrable while guested by an orb.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_09">Shiver me timbers, it could be breached by another, but... Alexander broke his, I mean me orb, a long time ago.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_10">Really? Well, if ye tell the truth, by all means. Seek out the pieces o' the broken orb and mend away.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_11">I believe he uses 'em fer torture now. They practically leak madness, which be quite useful I understand.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_TonicQuest_01">Daniel - I hate to bother ye further, but...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_TonicQuest_02">If ye be really goin' after Alexander. Would ye consider... takin' me with ye?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_TonicQuest_03">Blimey, I know it sounds ridiculous - I mean look at me. But if ye find anythin' concernin' a man named Johann Weyer, would ye please bring it to me?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_WeyerNote_01">Incredible - ye found Weyer's recipe. Then there might still be a chance.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_WeyerNote_02">Listen carefully. Alexander be workin' on openin' a gate - a door to another world. Avast, it be where he wants to go.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_WeyerNote_03">If ye could put yer anger aside, let him open the portal before ye take yer revenge. Shiver me timbers, let me pass the gate, Daniel.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_TonicQuest_04">I believe he was workin' on a way to help me. A recipe fer some sort o' grog - a tonic to free me from this husk o' mine.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_WeyerNote_04">Please, find the ingredients and prepare the tonic Weyer describes.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_WeyerNote_05">And do so before ye assemble the orb. The barrier keepin' ye from the inner sanctum will only be breached fer a short time. Unless everythin' be taken care o' before ye won't be able to save me.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Introduction_12">There should be six o' 'em. Look around the Choir and the Transept, ye should be able to find 'em there.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_LabLocked_01">So, the laboratory be locked. That be unfortunate. But it can wait. Find the orb pieces and the ingredients fer Weyer's tonic.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_LabLocked_02">We'll have to deal with the laboratory door later.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_PulledLever_02">There be machine parts hidden all over this place. Ye'll find a way to fix it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_PulledLever_01">What lever? Oh, that one. Har har, so many o' Alexander's things be breakin' down. Look around, maybe the other room.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_SafetyDoors_01">Shiver me timbers, ye got the doors open? Good goin'. I knew ye could do it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_MissedOrbs_01">I see ye have found some orb pieces, but there should be more. Alexander would most likely keep 'em close to torture contraptions.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_MissedOrbs_02">Check the Choir and Transept fer more.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_ChoirDone_01">Looks like ye cleaned out the Choir. Head fer the Transept and find the rest o' the orb pieces.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_TranseptDone_01">Ye seem to have found all the orb pieces used in the Transept. Go to the Choir and find the rest.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_AllOrbsNotIngred_01">Avast, I see ye have all the orb pieces ye need. I know I have no right to ask anythin' o' ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_AllOrbsNotIngred_02">But if ye can find it in yer heart to gather the ingredients fer Weyer's tonic before attemptin' to mend the orb, there might still be a chance fer ye to save me.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_AllOrbsNotIngred_03">Please, me fate be in yer hands.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_AllOrbs_01">Ye have everythin'. What be ye waitin' fer? Head towards the Chancel and find a way into the laboratory.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_AllOrbs_02">Inside, ye should be able to produce the tonic Weyer talked about.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random01_01">Who, me? I be Heinrich Cornelius Agrippa. I was once quite important, ye know.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random01_02">Baron Alexander has sustained me soul in this dead husk fer years. Who knows how many... hundreds I presume.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random02_01">Alexander be quite impressive in many ways. Yo ho ho, but he has grown impatient.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random03_01">Why me? I be the next best thing. Alexander really wanted none other than Johann Weyer.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random03_02">Yo ho ho, ye never heard o' Johann Weyer?! Me God, boy! He be probably the greatest man in history and ye don't know him?!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random03_03">Or be it the world who has forgotten him?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random04_01">Weyer was me pupil - me pupil.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random04_02">Aye, I do take pride in that fact. Be it so wrong?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random05_01">I found a Mithraeum once. One which had not been plundered. Do ye know o' Mithraism?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random05_02">I suppose it doesn't matter. It be an old faith buildin' temples out o' caverns. The dark walls inside bein' the universe and inside be its followers... humans watchin' the sky slowly turn.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random05_03">But the followers do have one thing to allow 'em a sense o' connection to creation... the Orbs.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random06_01">Shiver me timbers, not many orbs be left. They sometimes consume themselves or break when used by an uninitiated.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random06_02">Avast, I was lucky. The Orb I found spared me life and returned to where I had found it. I know, because Alexander took it and brought it to Brennenburg.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random07_01">Weyer was a brave man and dared to proceed where I did not. He unearthed a number o' cavern temples and gathered a whole collection o' Orbs.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random07_02">But unlike every other finder since the fall o' the Mithraic faith, he was able to unshackle the horror ye and I connect with the Orbs. He used 'em and was able to travel far and wide. Beyond the world itself.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random08_01">Me, powerful? Yo ho ho, not the way I had hoped fer. I have done all that I can to escape this brig, but now I use all me strength merely to stay alive.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random09_01">Me pupil, Johann Weyer, said he had found a way to take me with him beyond the stars.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random09_02">But I was too afraid to come along. Silly really... and now all I can do be regret it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random10_01">I have always hoped Weyer would return and give me a second chance. But so does Alexander, that be why he keeps me here... as a hostage in hope Weyer will reveal himself.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random11_01">Har har, ye be a good boy, Daniel, and I appreciate yer company, but I believe ye have more important things to care o'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Agrippa_Nrm_Random12_01">Shiver me timbers, ye should hurry, Daniel. No time fer sittin' around.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_Alexander_01">Daniel. Ye have gone too far. Blimey, I have to stop ye. I can't let ye proceed any further. I be sorry, me hearty.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_Alexander_01">Be this guilt I be witnessin', Daniel? If so, blame yerself. Ye started this.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_Alexander_02">Shiver me timbers, ye sent me that letter askin' fer help and this be how ye repay me? How dare ye?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_Alexander_01">Har har, what be me intentions, Daniel?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_Alexander_02">Salvation. It used to be yers, matey. But now ye only seek misplaced revenge. How do ye justify yer violence? Be it fer the greater good? Be ye doin' the world a service?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_Alexander_03">Har har, it be ye who caused all this pain and death. If ye had accepted yer fate and submitted to the Orb when yer first discovered it, none o' this would have happened.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_Alexander_04">Avast, it be curiosity in league with yer selfishness that be killin' us both.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L25_Alexander_01">Ye had me worried. Quite frankly, I be not sure what to do with ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L25_Alexander_02">I hold no grudge against ye, Daniel. We be so mighty much the same, ye and I.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L25_Alexander_03">Did ye really drink from the Amnesia mixture?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L25_Alexander_04">It does explain so much o' yer behavior. Ye never did finish what ye set out to do.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L25_Alexander_05">Ye talked about redemption... yarr. How ye would face the Orb's shadow and save our work - and me?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L25_Alexander_06">I will grant ye another chance to redeem yerself. Ye can wait here and stop the shadow.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L25_Alexander_07">Thank ye - matey.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_01">Avast, ye have to get out o' here...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_02">That taste... that fragrance... Damascus Rose.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_03">What... what be... this place?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_04">The darkness... closin' in...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_05">It be cold... it be so cold.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_06">Somethin' be wrong... oh, so wrong!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_07">There be nothin' left... everythin' be gone.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_08">The flicker... the bluish light.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_09">Gettin' closer... somehow.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_10">What was that?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_11">Someone's comin'...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_12">This shouldn't be...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01_DanielRamble_13">Be anyone there?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_01">What happened to her?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_02">Har har, maybe she knows...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_03">All dressed in blue...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_04">...that shimmerin' blue light.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_05">Just like Regent's Park.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_06">Be she dead?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_07">Help her. Find a way.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_08">Nay, don't kill her.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_09">The shadow... it be close now.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_10">Find her...!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_11">Get her back.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_12">She deserved it, that little... bitch.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_13">Do whatever it takes.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02_DanielRamble_14">Who be ye to question me?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_01">Shouldn't trust him.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_02">He be lyin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_03">Arr, he sees what I see.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_04">Get away, ye shouldn't do that!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_05">Should kill 'em all. Burn this castle to the ground.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_06">He'll never see it comin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_07">Crush his skull. He deserves it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03_DanielRamble_08">The blood... use it fer the ritual.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_Return_01">Daniel! I thought I had lost ye. The castle trembled and I could hear the Chancel collapse...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_Return_02">The laboratory might be accessible now.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_Return_03">Make haste. Ye be more than ready to make the tonic. Go on, ye should find everythin' ye need in the laboratory.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionNotStart_01">What be ye doin'? Time be runnin' short.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionNotStart_02">Hurry, ye'll find everythin' ye need in the laboratory.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionDone_01">Ye did it. Thank goodness!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionDone_02">Now, pay attention. First feed me the tonic and then use the saw to remove me head.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionDone_03">As the tonic begins to work ye will be able to cut off me head without takin' me life.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionDone_04">Then take me head and bring it with ye as ye enter the gate Alexander be openin' in the Inner Sanctum.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionDone_05">What do ye mean? Blimey, why wouldn't ye enter the gate?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionGiven_02">And Daniel, whatever happens - get me through that gate.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionDone_06">We can't argue now - ye need to act.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_SawNoPotion_01">Don't get ahead o' yerself. First we need the tonic.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_Agrippa_Nrm_PotionGiven_01">Quickly! Off with the head!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveHead_01">I was wonderin' if ye were goin' to show up.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveNoHead_01">Shiver me timbers, it saddens me to see ye filled with such hate. Be vengeance really what ye seek?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveNoHead_02">I hoped ye o' all could appreciate the grave nature o' the situation. After all, it has always been yer life we were fightin' fer.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveNoHead_03">Ain't it worth a little... sacrifice?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveNoHead_04">Come, help me finish the ritual. Avast, there be still time before the shadow catches up with ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveHead_02">I see Agrippa convinced ye to run some errands. Tell me, be everythin' nice and clear now? Be I the villain?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveHead_03">Good and evil. Such comfortin' concepts - but hardly applicable.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_ArriveHead_04">Be ye so blind that ye see no good in me? Or evil in Agrippa?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_AlmostDone_01">Har har, I realize, ye doubt me intentions. Why would I take such extreme measures to save yer life?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_AlmostDone_02">Maybe I be savin' mine too, matey.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_AlmostDone_03">I be just like ye, Daniel. A captive o' circumstance. Trapped in a world I no longer recognize.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_AlmostDone_04">As ye gain yer freedom, will ye deny me mine?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_AlmostDone_05">We be close now. Closer than I've been fer centuries.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_PortalOpens_01">Do ye see, Daniel? A whole other world - ain't it beautiful? Yo ho ho, I can finally return... home.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_PortalOpens_02">But ye... I be sorry Daniel. Ye won't be able to enter. Ye be still tainted - branded by the Shadow. Shiver me timbers, it will consume ye either way.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_Interrupt01_01">Nay, don't do that.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_Interrupt02_01">Stop it Daniel, ye be ruinin' it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_Interrupt02_02">We be so close - I beg ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_Interrupt03_01">Nay, ye bilge rat!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_Interrupt03_02">Ye killed us - ye killed us both!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Alexander_01">Thank ye, me hearty.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Alexander_02">Yer sacrifice won't be forgotten. Ye will be celebrated... forever.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_01">It was me greatest triumph.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_02">... and I never looked back.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_03">Ye think I was afraid fleein' Brennenburg? Quite the contrary.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_04">I knew that it was me purgatory - hellfire made to wash away me sins.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_05">There be no denyin' the things I've done. But I have paid me tribute. I gave 'em that awful man.., matey.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_06">... I did the right thing... yarr.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_AgrippaEnd_01">Nay, ye bilge rat! Blimey, ye have ruined us!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Agrippa_01">There he be. Do ye see him, Weyer? He deserves so much more.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Agrippa_02">Please help him, I know ye can.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Agrippa_03">Blimey, don't worry, Daniel. It will be alright.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_Cough">
        </Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Ending_Daniel_Scream">
        </Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L29_Alexander_DeathScream">
        </Entry>
    </CATEGORY>
    <CATEGORY Name="Flashbacks">
        <Entry Name="CH01L02_JourneyToSanctum01_01">Alexander, be it inside the castle?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L02_JourneyToSanctum01_02">In a manner o' speakin'. Come, bring the lamp. Ye've been to the refinery, have ye not?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L02_JourneyToSanctum01_03">I don't believe I have. Be it connected to the... what did ye call it?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L02_JourneyToSanctum01_04">The Inner Sanctum, me most precious chamber, Daniel. And it lies well beyond the refinery. In fact...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L02_JourneyToSanctum01_05">... it lies beneath the mighty stone o' Brennenburg.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_SecretBooks_01">Ye have to be swift - when ye activate the first one... ye hear that? Yarr, if it stops, ye'll have to start over.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_SecretBooks_02">Ain't all this a bit excessive?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_SecretBooks_03">Blimey, ye can never be too careful, Daniel.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_DanielDiary03_01">17th o' May 1839 - After poundin' the unforgivin' stone wall fer what seemed like an eternity, I realized it was hopeless. I was trapped.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_DanielDiary03_02">I fell to the ground gaspin' fer air, tryin' to focus. That be when I saw a faint blue shimmer.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_DanielDiary03_03">Me weakened body was heavy to carry but I managed to push meself toward the enchantin' light.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_DanielDiary03_04">It was waitin' fer me. Enclosed in dark nothingness, I felt meself drawn to the mystic light.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_DanielDiary03_05">I reached out, closin' it in me hands... yarr.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_DanielDiary03_06">Yo ho ho, the faint glow escaped me fingers and began to spark brightly and spirit me away. Unlockin' alien memories o' spiralin' towers, endless deserts, and impossible geometry.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_DanielDiary03_07">The next thing I can remember be the gratin' sound o' stone bein' lifted. The voices o' the Arabs pullin' me to safety. And grasped firmly in me hands was the broken pieces o' a most peculiar relic.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L04_CountChemistry_01">Shiver me timbers, there should be more cuprite.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L04_CountChemistry_02">And one part aqua fortis.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L05_Transformation01_01">Where did the baron go?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L05_Transformation01_02">Who cares? He left us enough rum to last us a lifetime. Or at least until tomorrow!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L05_Transformation02_01">What be happenin'? It feels like me chest be goin' to burst.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L05_Transformation02_02">Me God, Wilhelm, do somethin'... yarr!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L05_Transformation02_03">Accept it. Shiver me timbers, we be not gettin' out o' here alive.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L05_Transformation02_04">Yarr, how can ye say that?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L06_JourneyToSanctum02_01">Yo ho ho, it sure be dark in here.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L06_JourneyToSanctum02_02">Aye, and there be a good reason fer it. But ye can light the lamp now, if ye wish.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L06_JourneyToSanctum02_03">What be the reason? Fer the darkness, that be.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L06_JourneyToSanctum02_04">Stay close - be careful not to stray.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L06_JourneyToSanctum02_05">What be the reason? Why be it so dark?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L06_JourneyToSanctum02_06">Pay attention, Daniel. It be important that ye keep goin' straight and make sure not to stray.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L09_JourneyToSanctum03_01">Ye have an "ascendin' room". Will it take us to the Inner Sanctum?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L09_JourneyToSanctum03_02">It will definitely take care o' the vertical part o' our journey. So, ye have ridden an elevator before?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L09_JourneyToSanctum03_03">Aye, the Colosseum at Regent's Park has one. It takes ye to the gallery where ye can view the panorama.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L09_JourneyToSanctum03_04">Good. This ride might be a little longer - and in the other direction.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L10_DanielsMind01_01">Me captain's log be gone. Har har, what would they want with me captain's log?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L10_DanielsMind02_01">The key! Blimey, please, let it be here.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L10_DanielsMind03_01">Oh, thank God, there it be. I guess it be a good place to hide it, then.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L11_DogExperiment_01">Let's see what ye have to offer.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L11_DogExperiment_03">But I can sense it. It be definitely there.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L12_GirlChase01_01">Please, let me go. Har har, I won't tell anyone. I swear. I just want to go home.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L12_GirlChase02_01">Why be ye doin' this?! Get away from me!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L12_GirlChase03_01">Blimey, please, I beg ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Test01">Clarence curls curls</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Test02">ohhh ahhh don't stoooooooop</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L11_DogExperiment_02">What a mess, savvy. I should have sharpened the saw.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L00_DanielsMind01_01">Don't forget... some things mustn't be forgotten. The shadow huntin' me... I must hurry.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L00_DanielsMind02_01">Avast, me name be Daniel, I live in London at... at... Mayfair...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L00_DanielsMind03_01">What have I done? This be crazy. Don't forget, don't forget. Avast, I must stop him. Focus!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L00_DanielsMind04_01">Me name be...be... I be Daniel.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L12_GirlChase01_02">Nay, get away from me! Leave me alone!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L05_Transformation02_05">Alexander, ye piece o' shit! Har har, let us out o' here!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_JourneyToSanctum04_01">Come - this way, savvy.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_JourneyToSanctum04_02">Blimey, what was that?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_JourneyToSanctum04_03">Forgive me. I should have warned ye, matey. One o' me responsibilities as a baron be that o' a brig warden. This be where criminals be locked up.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_JourneyToSanctum04_04">Like a dungeon?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_JourneyToSanctum04_05">Mighty much so. Come - don't linger.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_Interrogation_01">Where be she? Where did she go?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_Interrogation_02">Nay, I won't tell. I'll never tell ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_Interrogation_03">Ye be just makin' things worse.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_Interrogation_04">Look - this be no place fer a young girl all by herself. She could be hurt or worse. There be no tellin' what horrors await down there.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_GirlEscape_01">But mother, I don't want to leave without ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_GirlEscape_02">Hurry child - ye must go. Find Gabriel the outrider and tell him to alert the king's men.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_GirlEscape_03">Nay, ye come too!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_GirlEscape_04">Please, we don't have time to make the hole any wider.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_GirlEscape_05">But --</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_GirlEscape_06">Someone be comin'. Hurry! I'll cover the hole with the bed. Everythin' will be fine - I promise.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_PrisonerCaptured_01">Hey! Anybody! Help!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_PrisonerCaptured_02">Christ - I don't believe this. Why... I mean why? What did I do to deserve this? I mean, it can't be... do I deserve this?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_PrisonerCaptured_03">It wasn't me fault!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L15_PrisonerCaptured_04">Shiver me timbers, why did he have to go in there? Ye don't go into burnin' houses. He should have known better.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L16_JourneyToSanctum05_01">So, ye use the drain sewers as a means o' transport?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L16_JourneyToSanctum05_02">Aye - they were built to divert water from an underground spring and be quite spacious.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L16_JourneyToSanctum05_03">It seemed only natural to incorporate it in the overall structure, arr.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L16_JourneyToSanctum05_04">But we won't be usin' it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L16_JourneyToSanctum05_05">Not today. The flow be seasonal and when the spring runs dry the damp tunnels produce a rather poisonous type o' fungi.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L16_JourneyToSanctum05_06">There be an antidote o' course - but we won't be botherin' with it today. Arr, come, this way instead. We be almost there.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L18_CisternVisit_01">Ye be conservin' water from the spring.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L18_CisternVisit_02">Aye, it enables me to control the water in the drain sewers to some extent. Also, it can be used fer all sorts o' purposes.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L18_CisternVisit_03">Like fer drinkin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L18_CisternVisit_04">Well, that too. But mostly to run different machines.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L18_CisternVisit_05">Ah, like water mills.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L18_CisternVisit_06">Exactly.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_01">Do ye see, Daniel? It has yielded.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_02">What?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_03">The shadow.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_04">It has?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_05">Fer now. Come. Let's get this out o' here so we can get some peace.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_06">Aye, let's. Where to?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_07">Just down the corridor, savvy. To the morgue.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_08">Be there more - dead men there?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_MorgueVisit_09">Ye did well, Daniel, arr. Come. Let's get goin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_FalseDeadPlague_01">What? What happened? Why be all these dead...? Where be I?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_FalseDeadPlague_02">What be happenin'?!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_FalseDeadPlague_03">Help! Anybody, help!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_FalseDeadPlague_04">Two... Three days now. This be ridiculous.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_FalseDeadPlague_05">Why doesn't someone come to this room?! Hey! Anybody!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_FalseDeadPlague_06">Be I all alone here? Help! Help!!!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L19_FalseDeadPlague_07">I be so tired..... yarr. If I sleep - will I wake from this nightmare? If not, I pray me heavenly Father will take me in me sleep.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L20_PrisonerTransported_01">What be happenin'?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L20_PrisonerTransported_02">What be ye doin'!? Let me go, arr!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L20_PrisonerTransported_03">Please don't take me - nobody ever returns...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_AlexanderAgrippa_01">Agrippa? Shiver me timbers, I need ye to stay awake. Can ye feel the syringe?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_AlexanderAgrippa_02">Nay, I can't feel anythin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_AlexanderAgrippa_03">Alexander?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_AlexanderAgrippa_04">Aye?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_AlexanderAgrippa_05">Soon I won't even be able to move, will I?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_AlexanderAgrippa_06">Arr, yer life be safe.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_AlexanderAgrippa_07">Shiver me timbers, I don't doubt that - but will it be worth livin'?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_WaitRoom_01">These cells be meant to hold captives who be under treatment. The people ye send fer will end up here.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_WaitRoom_02">Remember that the confinement itself works as a preamble to the torture and ye should pace yerself. Don't take anyone before they be ready.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_WaitRoom_03">Understood.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_WaitRoom_04">Sounds from the torture chambers be shuttled in through them pipes in the ceilin'. Manage yer victims well and let one captive's pain instill terror in his cellmate.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_PrisonerWaitRoom_01">I know this. I've been here already. I know this taste - the taste o' Damascus Rose obfuscatin' the truth in a dim haze.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_PrisonerWaitRoom_02">They may sweep the traces from me memory, but me body remembers, matey. These cuts speak volumes, even though me mind remains silent. They will be back.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L21_PrisonerWaitRoom_03">Oh, they will be back.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_MapRoom_01">Much o' the castle be old and hasn't been tended to fer centuries. When the Shadow arrives, it won't take long until things start fallin' apart.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_MapRoom_02">We be just buyin' time anyway. Let's do what we can.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_MapRoom_03">There ain't much to be done about the wards. We should reinforce weak structures. The ground will tremble and there be a risk everythin' will cave in on us - especially downstairs.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH01L03_MapRoom_04">Here... here... and there. Let's get the servants workin' on it.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_01">Just a little further.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_02">It be like Orpheus descendin' into the underworld.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_03">Be ye hidin' somethin'?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_04">What do ye mean?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_05">Never mind.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_06">Yer intuition be - remarkable.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_07">I be not sure I be followin'...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_08">It doesn't matter.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L22_JourneyToSanctum06_09">It's just a myth after all.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Escapee_01">Hey, ye. Stop!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Escapee_02">Don't come any closer! I just want to leave.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Escapee_03">Avast, ye can't go outside. It be too dangerous.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Escapee_04">I be tellin' Gabriel.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Escapee_05">I doubt that mighty much.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Nightmares_01">Daniel?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Nightmares_02">What?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Nightmares_03">Still havin' nightmares, I see.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Nightmares_04">Aye, I can't shake 'em. They come every night.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Nightmares_05">We'll put a stop to 'em. Ye'll see.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage01_01">Don't forget yer bag, Daniel.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage01_02">I won't, Herbert.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage01_03">There be no shame in usin' a parasol in the desert. As it happens, it be imperative to yer survival.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage01_04">But it looks ridiculous.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage01_05">The shame will hurt much less than dyin', I assure ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage02_01">Herbert, how did we find this place?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage02_02">An old matey back in Algiers gave me a map.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage02_03">Why ain't he with us? Didn't he want to come?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Random_Mirage02_04">He wanted to, Daniel. Yarr, but things don't always turn out the way we plan.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_TortureWheel_01">The wheel be good fer keepin' yer victim still durin' the procedure. They can be bound around the circumference or simply stretched across, tyin' limbs to the spokes and rim.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_TortureWheel_02">All tools be, by this point, useful and ye may administer the torture in any way ye like. But the forte o' the wheel be the gaps.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_TortureWheel_03">When ye have decided that the victim shall die ye can smash their limbs with a hammer, makin' 'em fold in between the frame.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_TortureWheel_04">But they'll die - too quickly I mean.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_TortureWheel_05">Nay, don't worry. The human body be much more resilient. They can survive fer days until they finally succumb.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerCage_01">How much more, Baron?! How much more be I supposed to withstand? Kill me already - kill me!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerCage_02">This one. Prepare him.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_01">Arr, let me go, ye brute!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_02">The Cradle be ready.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_03">Good.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_04">Ye? Ye be a man... how can ye partake in this?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_05">Be he alright?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_06">He be one o' the wicked. Don't pay his lies any attention, savvy.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_07">Har har, I be not a bad man. It was an accident...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_08">He set a man on fire... yarr.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_09">It wasn't me fault! Why won't anyone listen...</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_10">That be horrible... yarr.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerDragged_11">o' course - we be dealin' with monsters here.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerBeforeTorture_01">Nay, no, please. I'll do anythin'. Whatever ye want.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L23_PrisonerBeforeTorture_02">Anythin'... I'll do anythin'. Yo ho ho, I be innocent!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_01">15th o' August 1839 - The blood wards be failin'. The Shadow beckons and its cry disarms me actions.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_02">Hurry, no time to spare. Ye have to kill another.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_03">Alexander produces a knife. He wants me to cut the flesh.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_04">Avast, do it, save yerself. He be a murderer, Daniel. He be evil - a cold blooded killer.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_05">Hurry!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_06">Alexander, ye must let me be. I have to concentrate.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_07">Paint the man, cut the lines. Cut the flesh, watch the blood spill - let it come.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_08">Please, I didn't do anythin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_09">Paint the man, cut the lines. Paint the man, cut the lines.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_10">Please! the man cries.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_11">Hush, hush - now ye sleep.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_12">I did well. One life fer another. Ye hear me, Guardian o' the Orb, I did all this fer ye. Now, once more, withdraw yer shadow from me domain.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH02L24_DanielDiary07_03_13">Alexander. There ain't much time. I can feel it. We must act swiftly. I will do whatever it takes, savvy.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_DanielDiary08_01_01">18th o' August 1839 - Tonight we will unlock the power o' the Orb and ultimately banish the Shadow huntin' me.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_DanielDiary08_01_02">Har har, I feel it closin' in on me and I fear fer me life more than ever.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_DanielDiary08_01_03">Just outside Altstadt lies a small settlement where Zimmermann, a dairy farmer, lives with his wife and three children.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_DanielDiary08_01_04">We took the coach and went there. Avast, our visit was unexpected and Alexander was able to strike Herr Zimmermann down without alertin' the others.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="CH03L26_DanielDiary08_01_05">As he went to take care o' the farm hands, I began to look fer the children.</Entry>
