    <CATEGORY Name="EmotionStone">
        <Entry Name="Alexander01">One day I will return. If it wasn't fer the thought o' ye, me love, I wouldn't be able to go on. Avast, when I find meself doin' terrible things, I take comfort in ye. [br][br]As long as I be able to think o' ye and long fer a life together, I know I be better than the others. I weep fer 'em, they lust fer power without restraint, where I only crave fair judgment and a safe return.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Alexander02">When will it be me turn? Have I not shown restraint? Me patience spans centuries... yarr. From where I came, mankind be not even wasted a breath, yet I bow to ye. [br][br]I have done so much fer ye and I have gained nothin' in return. Agrippa, I trusted ye. Avast, it was I who in all fairness should have entered that gate.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Alexander03">I fear fer Daniel, fer he be reckless. He be tainted by the approachin' shadow and will not be able to pass the gate. Will he be able to accept this in the end? [br][br]Me love, I've seen evil in him. How be I to trust him with the truth? What cruel irony that I have to do unto him what Agrippa did unto me.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Alexander04">In court, the order o' the Black Eagle spew their politics at each other while I sit quietly in place, willfully forgotten. Once in a while someone will notice me and lose themselves in a silent cower before regainin' their senses.[br][br]Yarr, they all know I be the one and the same Alexander who helped their fathers and grandfathers to found this great Order. I've seen 'em take their fathers' places, and they too will grow old and pass away. While I remain the same, aged not by time, but by anguish.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Alexander05">Be it ye, me love, I miss the most, or be it perhaps meself? I know what I have become, I be not blind. I be a monster to 'em, a demonic sultan perched on a dark mountain top. There be little I can do to redeem meself.[br] [br]Shiver me timbers, the Black Eagle fears me and after Napoleon's defeat it be only a matter o' time before they will demand me head on a platter. I must remove meself from this land. This time it must work. If I can't return home now, I shall perish.</Entry>
    </CATEGORY>
    <CATEGORY Name="LoadingText">
        <Entry Name="Ch01_Beginning01">The door slammed shut behind him and he knew he would never again see the old tailor at Berkeley Square. Another lone soul in London - seemed appropriate somehow.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Ch01_Beginning02">The other children cheered him on. His name voiced in a steadily risin' pace, urgin' him to do it. "Be I really doin' this?", the young boy thought and struck his victim with a rock.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Ch01_Beginning03">He fell to the galley deck. Tears were beginnin' to well in his eyes as he received the first kick in his stomach. Hazel remained hidden, in fear she too would be punished.</Entry>
